        "source_sentence": "The melamine amide polymer exhibits the highest thermal stability, since its decomposition starts at ${ \\approx } 2 0 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$and gradual degradation occurs up to $3 0 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } ;$then complete decomposition takes place up to $4 8 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } .$The thermal stability of the p-phenylenediamine polymer is lower than that of the melamine one, since the decomposition begins at ${ \\approx } 1 6 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } ,$and after $2 5 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$the complete degradation occurs."
